  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I identified the following rule:\n\n1. Find all colored rectangles (hollow borders with either 0 or 2 interior)\n2. Rectangles with 2 in their interior are \"markers\" - always removed\n3. For each marker, check the shape of the 2-pattern inside: if height \u2265 width, the marker \"shoots upward\" and removes the nearest hollow rectangle directly above it (with overlapping columns)\n4. If the 2-pattern is strictly wider than tall (horizontal), the marker only removes itself\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    from collections import deque\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    visited = [[False]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    components = []\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] not in (0, 2) and not visited[r][c]:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                queue = deque([(r, c)])\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                cells = [(r, c)]\n                while queue:\n                    cr, cc = queue.popleft()\n                    for dr, dc in [(-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)]:\n                        nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == color:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            queue.append((nr, nc))\n                            cells.append((nr, nc))\n                min_r = min(r for r, c in cells)\n                max_r = max(r for r, c in cells)\n                min_c = min(c for r, c in cells)\n                max_c = max(c for r, c in cells)\n                \n                two_cells = []\n                for ir in range(min_r+1, max_r):\n                    for ic in range(min_c+1, max_c):\n                        if grid[ir][ic] == 2:\n                            two_cells.append((ir, ic))\n                \n                is_marker = len(two_cells) > 0\n                shoots = False\n                if is_marker:\n                    min_2r = min(r for r, c in two_cells)\n                    max_2r = max(r for r, c in two_cells)\n                    min_2c = min(c for r, c in two_cells)\n                    max_2c = max(c for r, c in two_cells)\n                    h = max_2r - min_2r + 1\n                    w = max_2c - min_2c + 1\n                    shoots = h >= w\n                \n                components.append({\n                    'color': color,\n                    'cells': cells,\n                    'min_r': min_r, 'max_r': max_r,\n                    'min_c': min_c, 'max_c': max_c,\n                    'is_marker': is_marker,\n                    'shoots': shoots\n                })\n    \n    to_remove = set()\n    for i, rect in enumerate(components):\n        if rect['is_marker']:\n            to_remove.add(i)\n    \n    for i, rect in enumerate(components):\n        if rect['is_marker'] and rect['shoots']:\n            best_j = None\n            best_dist = float('inf')\n            for j, other in enumerate(components):\n                if other['is_marker']:\n                    continue\n                if other['max_r'] < rect['min_r']:\n                    col_overlap = min(rect['max_c'], other['max_c']) - max(rect['min_c'], other['min_c']) + 1\n                    if col_overlap > 0:\n                        dist = rect['min_r'] - other['max_r']\n                        if dist < best_dist:\n                            best_dist = dist\n                            best_j = j\n            if best_j is not None:\n                to_remove.add(best_j)\n    \n    output = [[0]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    for i, comp in enumerate(components):\n        if i not in to_remove:\n            for r, c in comp['cells']:\n                output[r][c] = comp['color']\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    from collections import deque\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    visited = [[False]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    components = []\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] not in (0, 2) and not visited[r][c]:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                queue = deque([(r, c)])\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                cells = [(r, c)]\n                while queue:\n                    cr, cc = queue.popleft()\n                    for dr, dc in [(-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)]:\n                        nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == color:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            queue.append((nr, nc))\n                            cells.append((nr, nc))\n                min_r = min(r for r, c in cells)\n                max_r = max(r for r, c in cells)\n                min_c = min(c for r, c in cells)\n                max_c = max(c for r, c in cells)\n                \n                two_cells = []\n                for ir in range(min_r+1, max_r):\n                    for ic in range(min_c+1, max_c):\n                        if grid[ir][ic] == 2:\n                            two_cells.append((ir, ic))\n                \n                is_marker = len(two_cells) > 0\n                shoots = False\n                if is_marker:\n                    min_2r = min(r for r, c in two_cells)\n                    max_2r = max(r for r, c in two_cells)\n                    min_2c = min(c for r, c in two_cells)\n                    max_2c = max(c for r, c in two_cells)\n                    h = max_2r - min_2r + 1\n                    w = max_2c - min_2c + 1\n                    shoots = h >= w\n                \n                components.append({\n                    'color': color,\n                    'cells': cells,\n                    'min_r': min_r, 'max_r': max_r,\n                    'min_c': min_c, 'max_c': max_c,\n                    'is_marker': is_marker,\n                    'shoots': shoots\n                })\n    \n    to_remove = set()\n    for i, rect in enumerate(components):\n        if rect['is_marker']:\n            to_remove.add(i)\n    \n    for i, rect in enumerate(components):\n        if rect['is_marker'] and rect['shoots']:\n            best_j = None\n            best_dist = float('inf')\n            for j, other in enumerate(components):\n                if other['is_marker']:\n                    continue\n                if other['max_r'] < rect['min_r']:\n                    col_overlap = min(rect['max_c'], other['max_c']) - max(rect['min_c'], other['min_c']) + 1\n                    if col_overlap > 0:\n                        dist = rect['min_r'] - other['max_r']\n                        if dist < best_dist:\n                            best_dist = dist\n                            best_j = j\n            if best_j is not None:\n                to_remove.add(best_j)\n    \n    output = [[0]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    for i, comp in enumerate(components):\n        if i not in to_remove:\n            for r, c in comp['cells']:\n                output[r][c] = comp['color']\n    \n    return output",
